const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文考察大型高频做市商跨交易场所活动时的中介与库存特征。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"研究围绕可识别做市商的跨场所交易、报价和库存资料组织，而不是仅比较普通交易量。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"所需对象包括可识别交易商成交、场所级报价、库存或头寸代理、费用规则和跨场所同步时钟。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"该论文把新型做市商放入特定市场结构中讨论；它不证明所有算法化交易者都具有相同行为或作用。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"冻结交易场所名单、交易商分类、路由和费用制度，明确跨场所匹配规则，并记录数据是否包含暗池或内部化交易。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Financial Markets (2013)。缺少参与者身份、订单簿和场所级时钟时，不能将公开聚合行情解释为该论文意义上的做市活动。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Financial Markets (2013) for “High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.finmar.2013.06.006",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Markets (2013) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。缺少参与者身份、订单簿和场所级时钟时，不能将公开聚合行情解释为该论文意义上的做市活动。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “High Frequency Trading and the New Market Makers”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
